    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-v/q3",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q3-question-1.svg\" alt=\"At a college course 75% of the students are male and 25% are female. It is further known that 60% of the male students own a bike and 40% of the female students own a bike. A student is selected at random. Given that the student selected owns a bike determine the probability that this students is female ... a) ... by a two way table. ( ) 4 b) ... by a tree diagram. ( ) 4\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q3-question-2.svg\" alt=\"c) ... by a Venn diagram. ( ) 4\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q3-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"By tree diagram: Write F for female, M for male, and B for owning a bike:\" style=\"--madas-width:578.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q3-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) By a Venn diagram: A two-way table per 100 students is Bike No bike Total Male 45 30 75 Female 10 15 25 Total 55 45 100 [B1] [A1] The counts follow from 75(0.60) = 45 male owners and 25(0.40) = 10 female owners: Subtracting from the row totals gives 30 and 15 non-owners: Among the 55 bike owners, 10 are female, giving 2/11 . [M1] [A1] (b) In the tree, the female-and-bike path has probability 0.25(0.40) = 0.10, [B1] and the male-and-bike path has probability 0.75(0.60) = 0.45. [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:669.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q3-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"The probability is 0.10/(0.10 + 0.45) = 2/11 . [M1] [A1] (c) The intersection is 0.10, the F-only region 0.15, the B-only region 0.45, and the exterior 0.30. [B1] [A1] Therefore P(F | B) = 0.10/(0.10 + 0.45) . [M1] [A1] = 2/11\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 3 is 12 marks.</p>"
    ],
