      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q4-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Write O, L for an on-time or late train: The path probabilities refer to the 08:00, 09:00 and 10:00 trains in order: (i) The paths ending in O are OOO, OLO, LOO, LLO. [B1] [A1] The four path products are 0.93, (a) 0.9(0.1)(0.4), 0.1(0.4)(0.9) and 0.1(0.6)(0.4). Their sum is 0.729 + 0.036 + 0.036 + 0.024 = 0.825 . [M1] [A1] (ii) Exactly one O occurs on OLL, LOL, LLO, with probabilities 0.054, 0.004, 0.024. [B1] [A1] They total 0.082 . [M1] [A1] (b) The paths LOO, LLO have total probability 0.06. [B1] Dividing by 0.825 gives 4/55 ≈0.0727 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 4 is 11 marks.</p>"
