    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q5-question-1.svg\" alt=\"An airline operates between London and New York. The outward flight time, X hours, may be modelled by a Normal distribution with 7 2 hours and a standard deviation of 2 1 mean of 3 . a) Find the probability that one such flight will take more than 1 ( ) 8 2 hours. 3 The return flight time, Y hours, may also be modelled by a Normal distribution with mean µ hours and unknown standard deviation. P Y P Y Y b) Given that ( &lt; µ − 0.5 ) = 0.28 , determine ( &gt; µ + 0.5 &gt; µ − 0.5 ) . ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:578.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q5-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:577.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
