      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q5-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) The standardised cutoff is (8.5 −7.5)/(2/3) = 1.5. [M1] The probability is 1 −Φ(1.5) ≈0.0668 . [M1] [A1] (b) Symmetry gives P(Y &gt; µ + 0.5) = 0.28. [B1] The intersection is the whole upper-tail event, because every value above µ + 0.5 is also above µ −0.5. Its conditioning probability is 1 −0.28 = 0.72. The conditioning event has probability 0.72 and contains this upper tail, giving 0.28/0.72 = 7/18 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 5 is 6 marks.</p>"
