    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q10-question-1.svg\" alt=\"t = , relative to a fixed origin O , two particles, A and B , have position At time 0 a , respectively, where a is a constant. vectors ( i − 2 j + 4 k ) m and ( − 2 i + j + 6 k ) m It is further given that A and B , are travelling with constant velocities of ms− 1 ms− 1 ( 2 i + 3 j + 6 k ) and ( 3 i + 12 j + 4 k ) , respectively. The distance between A and B is least when t = 4s . Determine the value of a . ( ) 8\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
