    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-v/q11",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q11-question-1.svg\" alt=\"F 2 120° P F 1 F , of magnitude 24 N and x N The figure above shows two forces F and 1 2 respectively, acting on a particle P . The angle between the lines of action of F and F is 120°. 1 2\" style=\"--madas-width:556.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q11-question-2.svg\" alt=\"F is the force R , whose magnitude is  2x N . The resultant of F and 1 2 a) Show clearly that x = −+ ( ) 5 4 4 13 . b) Calculate the value of F − F , correct to three significant figures. ( ) 5 2 1\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q11-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Looking at the diagram below: In the force triangle, the included angle between the sides of lengths 24 and x is 60◦. [M1] By the cosine rule, (2x)2 = 242 + x2 −2(24)x cos 60◦. [A1] Simplifying gives 3x2 + 24x −576 = 0, or x2 + 8x −192 = 0. [A1] Completing the square gives √ (x + 4)2 = 208, hence x = −4 ± 208. [A1] A force magnitude is positive, so\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q11-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"√ x = −4 + 4 13 . [A1] (b) Reverse F1 and add it to F2 as in the second diagram: [B1] In this triangle the included angle opposite the required length is 120◦. [A1] The cosine rule gives |F2 −F1|2 = x2 + 242 −2x(24) cos 120◦ [A1] = x2 + 576 + 24x. √ Substituting x = −4 + 4 13 gives |F2 −F1|2 ≈934.7553. [M1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
