    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q14-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Integrating from v(0) = 0 [M1] gives v = 4t −t2/4 for 0 ≤t ≤8. [A1] At t = 8, v = 16, [A1] and it remains 16 m s−1 [A1] for t &gt; 8. [A1] (b) The car first reaches maximum speed at 8 s . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:670.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q14-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(c) Integrate 4t −t2/4 from the origin to obtain x = 2t2 −t3/12 [M1] [A1] for 0 ≤t ≤8. [M1] [A1] Then x(8) = 256/3, [A1] and x = 256/3 + 16(t −8) [A1] = 16t −128/3 for t &gt; 8 . [A1] (d) The distance remaining after eight seconds is 1000 −256/3 = 2744/3 metres: At 16 metres per second that takes 343/6 further seconds; add the initial 8 seconds: The position 1000 is reached in the constant-speed phase: Solve 16t −128/3 = 1000 [M1] to get t = 391/6 s ≈65.17 s . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
