    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q16-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A particle is projected from a point A , down the line of greatest slope of a smooth ms−. 2 incline plane and moves along a straight line with constant acceleration of 7.84 The particle experiences a constant normal reaction force of magnitude 29.4 N , throughout its motion. a) Determine the mass of the particle. ( ) 6 The particle reaches the point B , 2.5 s  after being projected and the point C , 2.5 s after passing through B . b) Given further that the distance BC is 100 m greater than the distance AB , find the projection speed and the distance AB . ( ) 8\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q16-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q16-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) With slope angle θ, g sin θ = 7.84, [B1] so sin θ = 0.8 [A1] and cos θ = 0.6. [A1] The normal reaction is mg cos θ = 29.4, [A1] hence m = 5 kg . [M1] [A1] (b) If the launch speed is u, then AB = 2.5u + 24.5 [B1] [A1] and AC = 5u + 98, in metres: [A1] Use 2(7.84)t2 twice: s = ut + 1 The gravity terms are 3.92(2.5)2 = 24.5 for AB and 3.92(5)2 = 98 for AC.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-v/q16-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Since BC = AC −AB = 100, 2.5u + 73.5 = 100. [A1] Thus u = 10.6 m s−1 [M1] [A1] and AB = 51 m . [M1] [A1] Source correction. The printed condition BC −AB = 100 is impossible: for consecutive 2.5-second intervals the difference is always 7.84(2.5)2 = 49 m. The handwritten working uses AC = AB + 100, equivalent to BC = 100.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 16 is 14 marks.</p>"
    ],
